### Description

@lgrammel @nicoalbanese When using the human-in-the-loop example, adding the ⁠`onFinish` callback to the ⁠`createUIMessageStream` function causes an infinite loop, resulting in the following error message being repeatedly printed:

```
@example/next-openai:dev: Error: failed to pipe response] {
@example/next-openai:dev:   [cause]: Error: tool-output-error must be preceded by a tool-input-available
@example/next-openai:dev:       at getToolInvocation (../src/ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts:108:20)
@example/next-openai:dev:       at eval (../src/ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts:502:39)
@example/next-openai:dev:       at runUpdateMessageJob (../src/ui-message-stream/handle-ui-message-stream-finish.ts:89:10)
@example/next-openai:dev:       at Object.transform (../src/ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts:99:14)
@example/next-openai:dev:       at Object.transform (../src/ui-message-stream/handle-ui-message-stream-finish.ts:67:19)
```

To reproduce the issue:

1. Clone the `vercel/ai` repository
2. Open the `examples/next-openai/app/api/use-chat-human-in-the-loop/route.ts` file
3. Add `onFinish: async () => {console.log('Done')}` to the `createUIMessageStream` function
4. Run the `next-openai` example in development.
5. Navigate to http://localhost:3000/use-chat-human-in-the-loop
6. Enter `What is the weather in SF?` into the chat
7. Press `Yes` to confirm
8. Watch the infinite loop / error in the terminal

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4d58ae4-f51c-49d1-9b01-c4c61a59f997

### AI SDK Version

- ai: 5.0.0
- @ai-sdk/azure: 2.0.0
- @ai-sdk/react: 2.0.0
